      "body": "\r\n\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nThe gRPC protobuf contract documents `max_new_tokens=0` as a 20-token default. However, the request converter previously left the internal `max_tokens` unset when `max_new_tokens` was zero or `stopping` was omitted. Downstream processing could then use a model default or the entire remaining context capacity.\r\n\r\n  Initialize gRPC sampling parameters with `max_tokens=20`. Existing positive `max_new_tokens` values continue to override the default.\r\n\r\n  The resulting behavior is:\r\n\r\n  - Omitted `stopping` → `max_tokens=20`\r\n  - `max_new_tokens=0` → `max_tokens=20`\r\n  - Positive `max_new_tokens` → preserve the requested value\r\n\r\nThis prevents unexpectedly large generation budgets and makes runtime behavior match the published protobuf contract.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n```\r\ncargo nextest run -p vllm-server \\\r\n    'grpc::convert::tests::absent_stopping_defaults_max_new_tokens_to_twenty' \\\r\n    'grpc::convert::tests::zero_max_new_tokens_defaults_to_twenty' \\\r\n    'grpc::convert::tests::positive_max_new_tokens_is_preserved'\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
